## Interface: 16001, 120105
## Title: Sane UI
## Notes: A sane user interface, built in modules. This is the part every module needs, with Sane UI's options (Esc > Options > AddOns > Sane UI, or /sane options) and the game settings it keeps the same on all your characters. The modules are listed below it: switch each one on or off by itself. Type /sane.
## Author: Saneroki
## Version: 0.3.0
## Category: Sane UI
## SavedVariables: SaneUIDB, SaneUIData_Characters, SaneUIData_Guild, SaneUIData_Learned, SaneUIData_Shared
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: SaneUICharDB
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Gear_01
## AddonCompartmentFunc: SaneUI_OnAddonCompartmentClick
## X-License: MIT

# Core is the addon every module depends on. Saved.lua describes the settings of all of them,
# Profiles.lua keeps them: in a profile (Speedleveling, Accountwide, your own) or a character's own (Character specific).
Core.lua
# Small helpers for every module: the game's words, colours, pixels, tooltips, pools, dialogs, fonts,
# sounds, and frames of the game's lent for a while
Kit.lua
# Distances and the time of day as the setting Units says: meters and 24 hours, or yards and 12 hours
Units.lua
# Plain values as a line of text and back (a profile to share)
Serial.lua
# The kinds of motion a window's size can have (Glide, Swing, Even, Instant): before Saved.lua,
# which describes the general switch that chooses one
Motion.lua
Saved.lua
Presets.lua
Profiles.lua
# What every window can use: places at the screen's edges to dock to, Esc, a watch on the mouse, a plate with
# round corners, background and border, moving (by a title bar, or in Blizzard's Edit Mode, chosen there with its
# dialog) and sizing (in Edit Mode), opening under the mouse, filling the screen from its screen edge, a title bar
# with a fuzzy search, views behind tabs, the game's own window kept out of sight while ours is chosen (the
# holder), a window not ours seated in a room of a full one (the seat), and a progress bar
Dock.lua
EditMode.lua
Escape.lua
Watch.lua
Fuzzy.lua
Shape.lua
Skin.lua
# Sane UI's own look: the journal of paper bound in leather, pencil on the paper, Kalam (Art/Journal, Fonts)
Journal.lua
Edge.lua
Window.lua
Classic.lua
Views.lua
Selection.lua
Holder.lua
Seat.lua
# What every health bar shows besides the health: the barrier, the lost maximum health, what can be dispelled
HealthMarks.lua
# A module's full screen of windows, laid out as the player arranges them, in layouts behind tabs
Board.lua
Expand.lua
Bar.lua
# The other addons Sane UI knows and adapts to when they are installed (the one file that names them)
Neighbours.lua
# Quick switches the modules offer, for a view that gathers them (the minimap's satchel)
Switches.lua
# The way to a place, for a module that leads the player, from the one that finds ways
Ways.lua
# The stats as players write them (Str, Stam, Crit), for every view that names one
Stats.lua
# Whether an item would make the character better, for the loot, the bags and quest rewards
Upgrade.lua
# The words of Sane UI's keys in the game's key bindings (what they do: Bindings.xml, read by the game itself)
Bindings.lua
# /sane window: a window to try them with
Demo.lua
# The data framework: Sane UI's own databases, and the scheduler that does their long work in steps, a few
# milliseconds a frame (Doc/guides/data.md). The sets themselves (Sets\<Set>.lua) are made by dev/tools/data
# from the master in assets/data and listed at the end of this file in the build; what Core keeps of the data
# in the game is in the saved variables SaneUIData_<Name> (Data.SAVED), what it learns in play in SaneUIData_Learned
Data\Steps.lua
Data\Codec.lua
Data\Data.lua
# What the data puts on a map: the places of Spawns, Places and Travel, per map (Data.Map)
Data\Map.lua
# The boats' and zeppelins' timetables, and when they sail on this realm, learnt on a ride (Data.Ships)
Data\Ships.lua
# The trip the player is on: a flight, a boat or zeppelin, the tram; its stops, how far along, how long (Data.Trips)
Data\Trips.lua
# Where the teleports of the set Travel bring one, learnt where one brought the player (Data.Learn)
Data\Teleports.lua
# What each of the account's characters has (bags, bank, worn), kept in the saved variable SaneUIData_Characters
Data\Characters.lua
# Sane UI's addon messages: the prefix, messages and blocks, a queue that keeps to the game's budget, the inbox (Core.Wire)
Data\Wire.lua
# The guild's records: the roster and its history, every member's records, shared with the guild (Data.Guild)
Data\Guild.lua
# What the game confirmed in play of the data not yet verified, kept and shared with the guild and the group (Data.Confirm)
Data\Confirm.lua
# What the game told in play, compared with the sets field by field: confirmed where it agrees, learned where not (Data.Check)
Data\Check.lua
# What play counts: loots and what they gave, places seen, per build period, for the harvest (Data.Tally)
Data\Tally.lua
# How often things come, for every view: the set Drops, this account's counts and the members' (Data.Drops)
Data\Drops.lua
# The discoveries, and the chat lines of them (Data.Found)
Data\Found.lua
# Core's watchers: creatures, things, mailboxes, crossings, a boss's loot and casts, the items' stats (Data.Watchers)
Data\Watchers.lua
# The quest watchers: offered, taken, worked on, handed in, compared with the set Quests (Data.QuestWatch)
Data\Quests.lua
# Every loot window counted: corpses, skinning, pockets, nodes, fishing, quest items, where (Data.Loot)
Data\Loot.lua
# Creatures, their services, vendors' goods, spells and the tooltips' items, compared with the sets (Data.Facts)
Data\Facts.lua
# What a thing fetches at the auction house for every view (Data.Series("Prices")), the full scan while it is open, every
# 16 minutes, kept in SaneUIData_Market, a file of its own (the addon SaneUI_AuctionData), and its bar on the game's window (Data.Scan)
Data\Rhythm.lua
Data\Prices.lua
Data\Fees.lua
Data\Scan.lua
Data\ScanBar.lua
# What a scan found told to this computer's other accounts while they run, by addon messages (Data.Relay)
Data\Relay.lua
# Counts and discoveries shared with the guild and the group, every 15 minutes (Data.Bundle)
Data\Bundle.lua
# Aliases and notes the player gives other players, set in the game's menu of a player (personal, never shared)
People.lua
# What the game says about a unit for every view: its quest objective, a player's item level and talents (paced inspections)
Objectives.lua
Inspect.lua
# Sync: the game's own settings kept with Sane UI's settings, a part per options page of the game
# and a few for what is on none (Edit Mode layout, chat windows, own channels). Pages.lua is made
# by dev/tools/sync-pages from Blizzard's options code.
Sync\Sync.lua
Sync\Data\Pages.lua
Sync\Layout.lua
Sync\Addons.lua
Sync\Keys.lua
Sync\Chat.lua
Sync\Game.lua
# Settings: the options, last: they show what everything above describes. The pages are put up
# at login, their controls made when the options are first opened.
Settings\Settings.lua
Settings\Panel.lua
Settings\Tabbed.lua
Settings\Screen.lua
Settings\Profiles.lua
Settings\Synced.lua
# The page Sane UI: links (Discord, website, GitHub) and feedback
Settings\About.lua
Settings\Data\CVarLabels.lua
Settings\CVars.lua
Settings\Banner.xml
Settings\CVars.xml
